Feature: GPU flag "skip_draws" (the emulated GPU draws nothing while a host renderer shows the game)

Applies to: rexglue-sdk nightly-20260921-923c1a59 (thirdparty/rexglue-sdk)
Apply with: git -C thirdparty/rexglue-sdk apply ../../patches/rexglue-sdk/0009-skip-draws-flag.patch
Status:     local patch (a feature for our port, not a bug fix)

WHY
  Our native renderer draws the game itself, but the emulated GPU kept
  drawing every frame too, even while nobody saw its picture: the native
  picture paid for BOTH renderers, and with the host GPU at ~97% busy the
  game waited on it (SwapBuffers ~15 ms/frame in busy scenes). The finished
  port turns the emulated GPU off; this flag lets us try that today.

WHAT
  A hot-reloadable bool flag skip_draws (default false) in the generic
  command processor: every draw packet (resolves are draws in "copy" EDRAM
  mode, so they're included) is still parsed and consumed, then skipped
  before IssueDraw. Everything else in the command stream keeps running
  (register writes, fences, interrupts, swaps), so the game never waits.
  The emulated picture then freezes / goes stale, and nothing is resolved
  back into guest memory.

HOW WE MEASURED IT (2026-09-30)
  Same save, jungle area of Wumpa Island, 60 fps cap: emulated picture
  only 69-96% GPU busy; native picture (both renderers) 97%, 56-57 fps;
  --native_only (this flag set while the native picture is shown) 15-20%
  busy, with the GPU clocking itself down (it has so little to do), 59 fps.
  Set by the game side through rex::cvar::SetFlagByName("skip_draws", ...)
  (src/native/native_renderer.cpp, UpdateEmulatedDrawing).

diff --git a/src/graphics/command_processor.cpp b/src/graphics/command_processor.cpp
index a744375..e85c0d0 100644
--- a/src/graphics/command_processor.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/command_processor.cpp
@@ -45,6 +45,16 @@ REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(clear_memory_page_state, true, "GPU",
 REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(occlusion_query_enable, true, "GPU", "Enable host occlusion query handling")
     .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kHotReload);
 
+// Mind over Recomp: lets a host renderer that draws the game by itself (the
+// port's native renderer) switch the emulated GPU's drawing off while its own
+// picture is on screen. Draw packets (and the resolves, which are draws in
+// copy mode) are still parsed and counted as done, so fences, interrupts and
+// swaps carry on and the game never waits; only the host GPU work is skipped.
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(skip_draws, false, "GPU",
+                    "Skip every draw and resolve (the emulated picture freezes / goes stale). "
+                    "For host renderers that draw the game themselves")
+    .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kHotReload);
+
 REXCVAR_DEFINE_STRING(readback_resolve, "none", "GPU",
                       "Controls CPU readback of render-to-texture resolve results.\n"
                       " none: Disable readback (default)\n"
@@ -1378,6 +1388,10 @@ bool CommandProcessor::ExecutePacketType3Draw(memory::RingBuffer* reader, uint32
 
       bool major_mode_explicit =
           xenos::IsMajorModeExplicit(vgt_draw_initiator.major_mode, vgt_draw_initiator.prim_type);
+      if (REXCVAR_GET(skip_draws)) {
+        // Nothing drawn, nothing resolved; the packet itself is consumed.
+        return true;
+      }
       draw_succeeded = IssueDraw(vgt_draw_initiator.prim_type, vgt_draw_initiator.num_indices,
                                  is_indexed ? &index_buffer_info : nullptr, major_mode_explicit);
       if (!draw_succeeded) {
